CAT = "nzfkRoad"; SEG = "RD"
# Forklifts on the road: the F endorsement and licence class (NZ Transport Agency Waka Kotahi).
Q = [
('What must a forklift operator hold to drive a forklift on a road?',
 'F endorsement on the licence', ['A forklift course certificate', "A WorkSafe operator's card", 'An HT class licence'],
 'NZ Transport Agency Waka Kotahi says anyone who drives a forklift on the road must have an F endorsement on their driver licence. A workplace course certificate alone does not cover road use.'),
('Which licence class, with an F endorsement, covers a forklift weighing up to 18,000 kg loaded?',
 'Class 1', ['Class 2', 'Class 4', 'Class 5'],
 'Waka Kotahi: a class 1 licence with an F endorsement covers forklifts up to 18,000 kg when loaded; over 18,000 kg loaded needs class 2.'),
('A container handler weighs 30,000 kg when loaded. What does its driver need for road use?',
 'Class 2 plus F endorsement', ['Class 1 plus F endorsement', 'Class 1 licence alone', 'Class 2 licence alone'],
 'Forklifts over 18,000 kg loaded need a class 2 licence with an F endorsement. 30,000 kg is well over that line, so class 1 is not enough.'),
('Which weight decides the licence class needed for a forklift on the road?',
 'Its weight including the load', ['Its empty weight only', "The load's weight only", 'The rated capacity on the plate'],
 "Waka Kotahi sets the class by the forklift's weight including its load: class 1 to 18,000 kg loaded and class 2 above that."),
('A worker passes the approved F endorsement course. When may they first drive a forklift on the road?',
 "Once it's on their licence", ['As soon as they hold the certificate', 'After a week of yard practice', 'When their employer signs off'],
 'Waka Kotahi warns that the course certificate alone does not let you drive a forklift on the road: the endorsement must be on the driver licence.'),
('Which of these does Waka Kotahi count as a road for forklift rules?',
 'A public wharf', ['A locked private yard', 'A fenced warehouse floor', 'A gated storage shed'],
 'The transport definition of road is very broad: streets and highways, plus any place the public has access to, including wharves, beaches, bridges and road shoulders.'),
('A factory yard has no gate and the public can walk through it. What may it count as?',
 'A road', ['A private site only', 'A building interior', 'A closed work zone'],
 'Waka Kotahi notes a factory yard with no gate may fit the definition of a road, so road licensing and driver behaviour rules can apply to forklifts used there.'),
('When a forklift is driven on a road, which rules apply besides licensing?',
 'Registration and road rules', ["Only the site's own speed limit", 'Nothing beyond the F endorsement', "Only WorkSafe's forklift guidance"],
 'Waka Kotahi says that if you drive a forklift in an area that counts as a road, the rules on registration, licensing and general driver behaviour all apply.'),
('What does the approved F endorsement course cover?',
 'Driving a forklift on the road', ['All workplace health and safety duties', 'Carrying dangerous goods by road', 'Heavy truck driving skills'],
 'Waka Kotahi says the approved course covers driver licensing requirements: specialist knowledge and skills for driving a forklift safely on the road. Employers may require separate health and safety training.'),
('When does an F endorsement expire?',
 'With the driver licence', ['One year after issue', 'Three years after the course', 'Never, it has no expiry'],
 'Waka Kotahi says an F endorsement expires on the same date as the driver licence it is on.'),
('Which licence must a person hold to add an F endorsement in the usual way?',
 'NZ full driver licence', ['NZ learner car licence', 'International driving permit', 'NZ restricted car licence'],
 'The F endorsement application asks for a New Zealand full driver licence or two other forms of identification, the course certificate and an eyesight check.'),
('Besides the course certificate, which check is part of applying for an F endorsement?',
 'Eyesight check', ['Hearing test', 'Drug test', 'Practical yard test'],
 'Applicants have their eyesight checked or show an eyesight certificate when applying at a driver licensing agent.'),
('Where do you apply for an F endorsement?',
 'Licensing agent', ['WorkSafe office', 'NZQA online portal', 'Local council office'],
 'The F endorsement is applied for in person at a NZ Transport Agency Waka Kotahi driver licensing agent.'),
('Does an NZQA forklift skill standard on its own let the holder drive on a public road?',
 'No, an F endorsement is needed', ['Yes, for loads under 18,000 kg', 'Yes, during daylight only', 'Yes, within 1 km of the site'],
 'NZQA skill standard 40735 states that achieving it does not entitle the holder to operate a forklift on a public road; a full licence of the right class with an F endorsement is needed.'),
('A worker holds only a learner car licence. What does skill standard 40735 say they need to drive a forklift on the road?',
 'Full licence of the right class and F', ['Nothing beyond the skill standard', 'A restricted car licence only', 'A learner licence plus F'],
 "Skill standard 40735 says that to operate a forklift on a public road the operator must hold a full driver's licence of the appropriate class with the F endorsement."),
('A beach launch ramp has public access. Why might a forklift there need an F endorsed driver?',
 'Beaches can count as roads', ['Sand counts as a work site', 'Boats need the endorsement', 'Ramps are council property'],
 'Waka Kotahi lists beaches, riverbeds, reserve land and wharves among places that can be roads because the public has access to them.'),
]
